Z||000041||SpeedPhreak||02-14-2000||12:21 PM||||i didnt really read any of the topic in question...the religon topic correct?... mainly because i feel i dont have the knowledge to participate.  this is also the 1st day ive read this thread...maybe i should have done it sooner.<P>what i do want to do is reaffirm the fact that i believe (as does most everyone else) that this 1 of the "closest" forums on the net.  i visit several forums & none of them come close to the repoir & feeling of friendship we have here...sure they are for the most part very informative & helpful but it ends at that.  any thing else they may have is a big flame war.  here it is more than that.<P>i feel the off topic forum is great... as we have seen many of us have similar interests other than fieros.  on the same level we cant expect us to have EVERYTHING in common so naturally we are not 100% the same in our interests, we need to respect that.  for example i personally found the master card post very funny, im sure others didnt... maybe even offensive.  so what, dont look at it anymore.  ive found some post that i didnt agree with or did not interest me... instead of getting all uptight about i know that others here have an interest in them so i leave it alone... why waste energy flaming/critizing/getting mad at stuff when u could using that energy constructivly on say your fiero?<P>i would hate to loose the off topic board & i would hate to loose the friendly atmosphere around here...thats what keeps me coming here all day...refreshing a few times an hour.<P>although i could probably match the length of others posts in this thread i will leave it at that... cant we all just get along   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">?<P><p>[This message has been edited by SpeedPhreak (edited 02-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000042||stimpy||02-14-2000||08:26 PM||||Did I hear my name being called? Yes Patrick, you are correct on both counts, I am joking and if it gets your goat, weelll, bonus.  I do appreciate that you are a highly intelligent individual (deduced by the quality of your posts) but sometimes higly intelligent individuals take on an arrogance that I, personally find offensive. I did find it humorous to compare the number of posts (along with the sheer vitriol) in the motor oil thread vs the God thread. You sure know how to pick your battles. <BR>Do I dislike you or feel that you have nothing worthwhile to say? Absolutely not! But I think that a little introspection on the part of some members might be in order. I know I have been guilty of typing away in the heat of the moment, and once you hit send, goodnight Irene!<BR>Well, anyway P, now that I got your attention with my little jibes, I promise to let it rest. <BR>Peace Out and Happy Motoring!||||reg||1
Z||000044||Patrick||02-15-2000||05:15 AM||||<BR><B>stimpy</B>, I'm in a good mood as I type this out, so please try to keep that in mind. My comments or questions are NOT tinged with any sarcasm or venom. Possibly my pleasant exchange earlier in this thread with <B>Sage</B> has allowed me to mellow out. Anyway...<P>First, give me a little bit of credit. You did <I>not</I> hear your name being called. I took the high road and didn't use your name or even indicate what threads I was referring to.<P>To tell the truth, I thought your latest comments were funny. Sorry, you didn't get my goat.<P>"Vitriol". Good word. I had to look that one up. Not sure where or when I'll be able to use it, but at least I learned something today.<P>I'm usually the easiest going guy anyone would care to meet, but when I feel like I've been wronged (as I did in the "oil" thread), yes, I can get cranky. And yes, there are times I may even come across as being arrogant. I'm not pleased about that, but I think it would be rather difficult to express oneself effectively <I>under those conditions</I> and NOT come across as being somewhat arrogant. If I was to start acting that way under normal circumstances, I would be very disappointed in myself.<P>There's one thing that's unfortunately still bugging me. I don't understand why you appear to want to make peace, and then in reference to the "oil" and "God" threads you state, "You sure know how to pick your battles". To me that comes across like a real slap in the face. Please inform me if I've misinterpreted your comment. <P>Believe it or not, in the "oil" thread I made what was honestly an innocent joke. It's no point rehashing the whole thread, but when you lashed out at me, telling me among other things not to be so "freakin paranoid", well, the rest is history. Far from looking for a battle, I was initially trying to make you smile! In that thread I stated no less than three times that I just wanted to move on and/or forget about it. There is one other thing that is probably worthwhile mentioning. The subject heading of the email you sent to me was "shakin off the gloves". I have no idea what you actually meant by that, but Canadians (especially ones who play hockey, as I do) perceive the throwing off of gloves to be an invitation to fight. So you can see why I didn't view your email as much of a goodwill gesture, <I>if</I> that's what it was meant to be.<P>In regards to the "God" thread, I felt all along that it was an open invitation to disaster. I had no wish to actively participate in something that I could easily foresee was going to cause plenty of ill will among the participants. I'm glad I didn't say anything more than I did because I'm sure all hell would've broken loose. You see, I do have <I>some</I> common sense.<P><B>stimpy</B>, if you'd care to comment on anything I've mentioned here, I'd be more than willing to follow up on it again.||||reg||1
Z||000045||Monkeyman||02-15-2000||06:02 AM||||Let's not start fighting again.  I know.  Nobody was fighting, but I can see it comin'.  I don't want to be a referee (although B&W stripes look good on me.  At least that's what my cell mates tell me.)||||reg||1
Z||000046||stimpy||02-15-2000||06:49 AM||||Patrick. I do take some interpretive license when I write. Yes, I realize that you did not use my name.  I am not going to cower in the dark just because you didn't point the light my way. I know that I have been spreading some lighthearted wisecracks around, and I thought it would be proper to keep on tryin to clear the air.<BR>First off, everybody but you who has read that tiresome oil thread (How I rue the day I posted that one) realizes my paranoia reference was directed to shiner. Shiner and I have communicated off-forum and it ain't no big deal. <BR>Secondly, as a hockey fan myself, I am fully aware of what shakin off the gloves means. It's all entertainment, no one dies, and everyone hugs each other at the All-Star game.  My emai was about venting some steam, "if ya got something to say,bring it on." That kinda thing.<BR>Patrick, if I was the only one who thinks you come off as what you purport to detest, (arrogant) then I would keep my mouth shut.  But having received several emails during our past coup d'etat supporting me, think of this as good ol fashioned intervention. <BR>Patrick, we are your friends and we love you. It hurts us to see you living in denial, and we want you to get help.<BR>Paix Sortir <BR>ton ami<BR>stimpy||||reg||1
